results.theorem:
Let $\varphi$ be a quasi-psh function on a Hermitian manifold $(M,\omega)$. Let $\gamma$ be a continuous real $(1,1)$-form on $M$ such that $\sqrt{-1}\partial ar{\partial}\varphi\geqslant\gamma$ and let $\eta$ be a continuous function on $M$ so that $\eta>\varphi$. Then for any relatively compact open set $D\Subset M$, there exists a decreasing sequence $\{\varphi_{
u}\}_{
u=1}^{\infty}$ of quasi-psh functions on $D$ satisfying the following properties:


(1) $\varphi_{
u}<\eta$ on $D$ for $
u\gg 1$ and $\lim_{
uightarrow+\infty}\varphi_{
u}=\varphi$;


(2) $\varphi_{
u}\in C^{\infty}(D ackslash S_{
u})$ and $S_{
u}:=\varphi_{
u}^{-1}(-\infty)$ is a closed analytic subset of $D$;


(3) $\sqrt{-1}\partial ar{\partial}\varphi_{
u}\geqslant\gamma-\delta_{
u}\omega$, in which $\delta_{
u}$ are positive constants so that $\delta_{
u}	o 0$;


(4) (equisingular) for every $t>0$, $\mathcal{I}(t\varphi)|_{D}=\mathcal{I}(t\varphi_{
u})$ for $
u\gg 1$.
